Fiber to the Home (FTTH)
    - Fiber optic connection brought directly to individual residences
    - Highest speed and reliability

Fiber to the Curb/Cabinet (FTTC)
    - Runs to the curbside or cabinent and use traditional copper cable for individual homes or buisnesses
    - Strikes balance between cost and performance

Fiber to the Node/Neighborhood (FTTN)
    - Extended to a central point in a particular area or neighborhood
    - Allows service providers to leverage existing copper infrastructure that offers improved speeds

Fiber to the Building/Basement (FTTB)
    - Fiber optic cables reach the building's main communication room or basement



